body:
This issue which @davidkyle hit locally:

```
   > Caused by: java.lang.NullPointerException
   >    at java.base/sun.security.ssl.SSLSessionImpl.getLocalPrincipal(SSLSessionImpl.java:661)
```

should be fixed. There was a [bug](https://bugs.java.com/bugdatabase/view_bug.do?bug_id=8206355) in earlier JDK11 builds that's fixed in ea22.

However the issue that CI is reporting is a failure to do with getting sessions by id.

This code:
```
       private void invalidateSessions(SSLSessionContext sslSessionContext) {
            Enumeration<byte[]> sessionIds = sslSessionContext.getIds();
            while (sessionIds.hasMoreElements()) {
                byte[] sessionId = sessionIds.nextElement();
                sslSessionContext.getSession(sessionId).invalidate();
            }
        }
```
is causing a NPE on the `getSession` which is strange since the ID came from `getIds` on the same object.

@jkakavas is investigating.

Words are hard, and I realise my previous question isn't 100% clear so for clarification...
If we had the following code:


      public void testSessions(SSLSessionContext sslSessionContext) {
            List<byte[]> sessionIds = Collections.list(sslSessionContext.getIds());
            for (byte[] sessionId : sessionIds) {
                SSLSession session = sslSessionContext.getSession(sessionId)
                Objects.requireNotNull(session); // <<- A
            }
            for (byte[] sessionId : sessionIds) {
                SSLSession session = sslSessionContext.getSession(sessionId)
                Objects.requireNotNull(session); // <<- B
                session.invalidate();
            }
        } 

would we see a failure at A or at B (on the 2nd iteration of the loop)?
